    "notes": "t17 is a control map: r scales the parallax offset of t3 and t4, g blends the parallax layers toward t2, b adds t2 to the emissive. The client samples t0 only where v3w > 0; lerp by 0 makes that the same. The simple-lighting programs (14-25) compute the same diffuse and no emissive. The emissive output is before the client's view-depth fade: after lighting it is scaled by saturate(v5.z * cb1[8].x + cb1[8].y) (SHADER_FINDINGS/notes/wmo.md). Alpha is what the shader alpha-tests (128/255, per MSAA sample)."
